  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Agricultural Model Intercomparison and Improvement Project (AgMIP)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">A 6-month landscaping project to identify demand, opportunities and capacity-building needs for enhanced agricultural climate modelling capability in 6 sub-Saharan African countries (Ethiopia, Ghana, Kenya, Nigeria, Senegal and Zimbabwe). AgMIP will support government stakeholders to model and understand the implications of policy and programming decisions linked to National Adaptation Plans, National Agricultural Investment Plans, Nationally Determined Contributions, and Biennial Transparency Reports. AgMIP will work with CGIAR-IFPRI to combine the strengths of their modelling tools to support low-emissions, climate-resilient agri-food systems and policy advancement.</narrative>
  </description>
